------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <ThemeProvider> is a TRANSPARENT context provider: it renders {children} and writes the active
palette to :root CSS vars + body.background + the color-scheme/dark class; it hydrates the selection
from localStorage synchronously, then from the backend /settings feed (raw fetch, .catch swallowed),
persists changes back (fire-and-forget PUT, gated on `initialized`), resolves `auto` against the system
appearance, and mirrors changes from other tabs without re-persisting/re-broadcasting. Its data source
is the `useTheme()` context. The native peer reproduces ALL of that, mapped to SwiftUI idioms:

  • Data source useTheme()  : EnvironmentValues.theme (read) + .themeController (write), provided by the
                              P1/S8 @Observable ThemeProviderModel — no HTTP in the view; every side
                              effect goes through an injected seam (persistence / remote / broadcaster).
  • 6 colorways + 7 modes    : ported 1:1 (every hex/rgba literal verbatim); each built-in colorway's
                              primaryRGB/accentRGB is pinned to the web precomputed string in AdapterTests.
  • custom                   : rebuilt from the live #00b4d8/#e63946-defaulted pair (web buildCustomTheme);
                              setCustomColors forces colorway=custom + broadcasts both messages.
  • auto                     : resolves to dark/light by ambient colorScheme (web systemDark), live via
                              .onChange(of: colorScheme); the selected id stays `auto` (web modeId).
  • localStorage             : UserDefaults under the verbatim keys teslasync-theme / -mode /
                              -custom-primary / -custom-accent.
  • /settings hydrate+persist: ThemeRemoteGateway seam (web first-mount fetch + fire-and-forget PUT);
                              backend save suppressed until the first hydrate resolves (web !initialized).
  • cross-tab broadcast      : ThemeBroadcaster (NotificationCenter) — publish on local change, mirror
                              received changes WITHOUT re-persist/re-broadcast (web subscribe guard).
  • states                   : the web hydrate is SILENT (never blocks render). ThemeSyncPhase makes that
                              lifecycle observable; ThemeSyncStatusBadge renders EVERY state — loading
                              (spinner), synced, local-only, stale (chip + refresh), failed (chip + Retry),
                              offline (chip) — so a host shows status without ever hiding the themed UI.
Shared comps : none (the web source composes none — it is a provider). Charts/maps: none -> Swift Charts /
               MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : colorway + mode display names mirrored verbatim from web themes/modes; status + swatch a11y
               are native additions; ALL resolved through the P1/S10 ThemeProviderStrings facade.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "ThemeProvider" (P1/S11).
a11y         : status badge is one combined element with a localized "Theme sync status: <x>" label +
               a labelled Retry; swatches are combined elements with localized labels + .isSelected;
               Dynamic Type via tokens; reduce-motion N/A (no motion); preferredColorScheme drives polarity.

